{{also|Bruno}}
==Italian==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ML.|it}} {{m|la|brūnus}} "brown, brunet" (whence also {{etyl|es|-}} {{m|es|bruno}}, {{etyl|fr|-}} {{m|fr|brun}}), from {{etyl|frk|it}} *{{m|frk||brūn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|it}} {{m|gem-pro|*brūnaz||brown}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|it}} {{m|ine-pro|*bher-||shining, brown}}. Akin to {{etyl|goh|-}} {{m|goh|brūn}} "brown" ({{etyl|de|-}} {{m|de|braun}} "brown"), {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|brūn}} "brown". More at {{l|en|brown}}.

===Adjective===
{{it-adj|brun}}

# (dark) [[brown]]

====Derived terms====
* [[orso bruno]]

===Noun===
{{it-noun|m|f=bruna}}

# a dark-haired person

